 "lineage_note": "Europe's second club cup. 1971-72 to 2008-09 = UEFA Cup; 2009-10 on = UEFA Europa League (same competition and records). The Inter-Cities Fairs Cup (1955-58 to 1970-71) is a different competition not organised by UEFA and is NOT included, although some sources list it as the forerunner. Finals were two-legged up to 1996-97 (aggregate shown, legs in notes, away goals noted); single match from 1997-98. Top scorer uses UEFA's convention: main-competition goals only (qualifying and play-off rounds excluded; from 2004-05 group/league phase to the final). Values are kept only where two of three sources agree (Wikipedia, RSSSF, UEFA's statistics database). Every season from 1971-72 now passes: UEFA and Wikipedia agree in every year, and RSSSF differs only in 1974-75 (Heynckes 10, not 11), 1984-85 (Bannister for Szabó), 1986-87 (adds Kieft) and 1993-94 (adds Edgar Schmitt). 2000-01 was settled with a third and fourth source: UEFA, weltfussball.de and Italian Wikipedia all give a four-way tie on 6 (Drulić, Kuźba, Javi Moreno, Nikolaidis); RSSSF's Berbatov/Pérez Alonso 7 appears to include qualifying-round goals. 2020-21 uses the four-way tie given by RSSSF and UEFA (Wikipedia's list leaves out Gerard Moreno). Top assister = UEFA's official assist count, continuous in UEFA's statistics database from 2001-02; UEFA holds no assists before that and no other source gives a full, agreed list for the 1990s.",
